Notebook[{

Cell[CellGroupData[{
Cell["Tree-level graviton scattering with FeynArts", 
      "Title", ExpressionUUID -> "14a74f86-b215-4b20-94e3-aff4e139f2e7"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Tree-level four-graviton scattering with FeynArts. The notebook works in \
three stages and gives every intermediate result a name, so any cell can be \
re-evaluated on its own.\n\nFirst it builds the complete 2 \[Rule] 2 tree \
amplitude off shell. FeynArts generates the three exchange diagrams and the \
four-graviton contact, the external polarisation tensors are attached as \
formal factorised tensors, and each diagram is contracted with FORM. The \
total is stored in theAmplitude[p1, p2, p3, p4].\n\nThen it imposes the \
massless on-shell kinematics: FCClearScalarProducts[] removes earlier \
scalar-product assignments, SetMandelstam fixes the momentum products ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["p", "i"], "\[CenterDot]", 
    SubscriptBox["p", "j"]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "0ad5eead-ef13-4b9b-9b7c-ed128a0a7b64"],
 ", and a block of Pair assignments fixes the polarisation contractions, \
namely transversality of each wavefunction, the null property ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "i"], "\[CenterDot]", 
     SubscriptBox["\[CurlyEpsilon]", "i"]}], "=", "0"}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "e72b63f8-3978-406a-ab35-91b086214c44"],
 ", and the polarisation-momentum and polarisation-polarisation tables.\n\n\
Finally it reduces the result to helicity amplitudes labelled by ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  FormBox[
   RowBox[{
    SubscriptBox["h", "1"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["h", "2"], ",", 
    SubscriptBox["h", "3"], ",", 
    RowBox[{
     SubscriptBox["h", "4"], "=", 
     RowBox[{"\[PlusMinus]", "1"}]}]}], TraditionalForm]],
  FormatType->TraditionalForm,ExpressionUUID->
  "24742372-3907-474b-b9be-e716a3d4cfb2"],
 " and compares four combinations with closed forms in s, t and u.\n\n\
Conventions: metric signature (+, -, -, -); FeynArts treats all external \
momenta as incoming, so the physical outgoing momenta p3 and p4 enter \
SetMandelstam as -p3 and -p4 and their polarisations carry the conjugated \
label -I. The gauge parameter is fixed at 2 by the model. No loop \
integration, spin sum or cross section is computed."
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000872346945178*^9, 
  4.0008724112242537`*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"dc7be9f0-e01f-482e-b16b-\
a401a43db518"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["1. Initialisation", "Section", 
         ExpressionUUID -> "66979d8e-122c-4326-a3d4-6b1c333b6c2c"],

Cell["\<\
Start with a fresh kernel (especially after running the previous on-shell \
version) and evaluate the two cells below with Shift+Enter. The first loads \
FeynGrav, which loads FeynCalc and CalcFormConverter, and asks FeynCalc to \
load the installed patched FeynArts. The saved pure-GR model uses gauge \
parameter 2 and contains the cubic and quartic graviton interactions and \
gravitational ghosts. GenericModel is given explicitly because the classes \
file does not name its generic model and the FeynArts default is the stock \
\"Lorentz\" file. No diagrams are generated and FORM is not executed here. \
Opening this notebook executes nothing.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"3f444fd2-0054-4d3a-9b81-971cc7884bc8"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[{
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"$LoadAddOns", "=", 
   RowBox[{"{", "\"\<FeynArts\>\"", "}"}]}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"<<", "\"\<FeynGrav`\>\""}], ";"}], "\n", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"grModel", "=", "\"\<PureGR\>\""}], ";"}], "\[IndentingNewLine]", 
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"InitializeModel", "[", 
   RowBox[{"grModel", ",", 
    RowBox[{"GenericModel", "\[Rule]", "grModel"}]}], "]"}], ";"}]}], "Code",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{4.00081504920359*^9, 4.000866046683724*^9},
 CellLabel->"In[1]:=",ExpressionUUID->"2da8c400-44f9-4e33-b46c-24d635d8fb3d"],

