Cell["\<\
PolarizationTensorD represents the formal factorised tensor epsilon^mu \
epsilon^nu. Neither p.epsilon nor epsilon.epsilon is set to zero; no \
normalisation or helicity is chosen. I and -I specify incoming polarisations \
and conjugated outgoing polarisations, not helicities.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"12c3725a-e338-47f6-af42-3770b19c9779"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{"externalTensors", "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{"PolarizationTensorD", "[", 
     RowBox[{"p1", ",", "\[Mu]1", ",", "\[Nu]1", ",", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], 
     "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"PolarizationTensorD", "[", 
     RowBox[{"p2", ",", "\[Mu]2", ",", "\[Nu]2", ",", "\[ImaginaryI]"}], 
     "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"PolarizationTensorD", "[", 
     RowBox[{"p3", ",", "\[Mu]3", ",", "\[Nu]3", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}]}], "]"}], " ", 
    RowBox[{"PolarizationTensorD", "[", 
     RowBox[{"p4", ",", "\[Mu]4", ",", "\[Nu]4", ",", 
      RowBox[{"-", "\[ImaginaryI]"}]}], "]"}]}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000815787333487*^9, 4.00081581360179*^9}, {
  4.000818110670472*^9, 4.0008181318058863`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[8]:=",ExpressionUUID->"292e61ba-7c0b-4706-879e-3651b86b9c85"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["4. Form the total off-shell amplitude", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"6f6a6ff3-9c0d-44ad-aa3e-184e1d958b39"],

Cell["\<\
Contract the diagrams separately with FORM to limit intermediate expression \
sizes. Each contraction uses CalcFormCalculate with its default options: the \
Lorentz dimension is inferred from the expression, which carries symbolic D, \
and successful FORM jobs are cleaned up automatically. No scalar-product \
assignments, helicity tables, mass-shell conditions or extra graph factors \
are introduced.

The four contracted diagrams are summed immediately into theAmplitude[p1, p2, \
p3, p4]. The momenta are arguments of that definition, so a permuted \
evaluation, for instance the exchange of the two incoming legs, can be formed \
later from the same stored expression.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"f555f0c6-1f7b-41fa-96e0-e41d00c29ecc"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"theAmplitude", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p1_", ",", "p2_", ",", "p3_", ",", "p4_"}], "]"}], "=", 
   RowBox[{
    RowBox[{
     RowBox[{"(", 
      RowBox[{
       RowBox[{"CalcFormCalculate", "[", 
        RowBox[{
         RowBox[{"FeynAmpDenominatorExplicit", "[", "#1", "]"}], " ", 
         "externalTensors"}], "]"}], "&"}], ")"}], "/@", "diagramTensors"}], "//",
     "Total"}]}], ";"}]], "Input",
 InitializationCell->False,
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000817255306489*^9, 4.000817259238511*^9}, {
  4.000817545853169*^9, 4.00081755040644*^9}, {4.000817694794487*^9, 
  4.0008177195108356`*^9}},
 CellLabel->"In[9]:=",ExpressionUUID->"571a1c11-feb5-4f90-af0c-802cd772764d"],

Cell["\<\
theAmplitude[p1, p2, p3, p4] now holds the complete polarisation-contracted, \
amputated off-shell tree expression: all four diagrams with their graph \
factors, and still with unconstrained external virtualities, longitudinal \
contractions and trace terms.

Short shows only a preview and Length counts the terms of the stored \
expression; neither changes it. This is not yet an on-shell scattering \
amplitude, and it contains no loop measure or spin sum.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.000817266878055*^9, 4.000817267051003*^9}, {
  4.000817323113295*^9, 
  4.000817323283*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"460c06eb-23a9-45da-93f4-23d0e7b522bf"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Short", "[", 
  RowBox[{
   RowBox[{"theAmplitude", "[", 
    RowBox[{"p1", ",", "p2", ",", "p3", ",", "p4"}], "]"}], ",", "4"}], 
  "]"}]], "Input",
